e + N2(X) -> e + N2(w_1Delta_u). Su et al. J. Phys. B 54, 115203 (2021) (CC BY 4.0) below 20 eV; Johnson et al. J. Geophys. Res. 110, A11311 (2005) Table 2 from 20 eV; power-law continuation p = 0.53 above Johnson's last point (to 10 keV). Overlap Su/Johnson: 12.5 eV 3.82 (+-0.36), 15 eV 1.02 (+-0.19), 17.5 eV 1.41 (+-0.19), 20 eV 1.34 (+-0.19); step at 20 eV Su/Johnson = 1.34. Continuation share of the rate: T_e 20 eV 1.5 % (zero/hold tail -1.5/+0.2 %), T_e 30 eV 6.7 % (zero/hold tail -6.7/+1.0 %). Header 10.27 eV = experimental vertical excitation energy (Oddershede, Su 2021 Table 1); no threshold shift. Maxwellian-integrated by abep_sim/rate_tables.py (scripts/build_n2_electronic_excitation_tables.py). Reaction set abep-n2n-0.9.
